      "writtenOn": "2018-03-22T11:25:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so at the end of the day :\nn \u003d DIV_ROUND_UP(len , 4);\n\nis there really something to do for the special case you mentioned (n\u003d0) ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 111,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 111,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "599bfa777053ed93db64d27930f0fd4b49d819d1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2c48a9a0_7a5fd1e1",
        "filename": "chip/g/dcrypto/aes_cmac.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1264944
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-03-28T12:30:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, if n \u003d 0 then we want to set n \u003d 1 and flag \u003d 0. The flag tells us whether the last 128-bit block of the input is complete, or if we have to pad it. So, for instance, if len\u003d16, we have 128 bits of input, so we set n \u003d ceil(16 / 16) \u003d 1 and flag \u003d 1 to declare one block, which is complete. But if len\u003d0, we do not want n \u003d ceil (0 / 16) \u003d 0 and flag \u003d 1; instead, we want to special-case this and treat it as a single incomplete block by setting n \u003d 1 and flag \u003d 0.\n\nPerhaps, though, this would be clearer with a separate if statement that just checks if len \u003d 0 and adds the special case?",
      "parentUuid": "5aea6a8c_2a6f02c1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 111,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 111,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "599bfa777053ed93db64d27930f0fd4b49d819d1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61d73423_b7b90899",
        "filename": "chip/g/dcrypto/aes_cmac.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000016
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-03T09:29:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes we should probably put a len \u003d\u003d 0 conditional at the beginning and be done with it.",
      "parentUuid": "2c48a9a0_7a5fd1e1",
      "range": {
